## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement a realistic, offline-capable data layer for map UI, with viewport-aware rendering and incremental updates.

## Key Concepts

- Offline caching with AsyncStorage or MMKV
- Viewport-filtered rendering using react-native-maps Region
- Throttling network calls to avoid floods
- Merging remote updates into local cache
- Hook design pattern for region-driven data updates

## Code Example

```javascript
import { useEffect, useState, useRef } from 'react'
import AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage'
import { fetchMarkersForRegion } from './api'

export function useViewportMarkers(region) {
  const [markers, setMarkers] = useState([])
  const lastRegion = useRef(null)
  useEffect(() => {
    let mounted = true
    const key = JSON.stringify(region)
    if (!region) return
    const fetchIfNeeded = async () => {
      if (lastRegion.current === key) return
      lastRegion.current = key
      const data = await fetchMarkersForRegion(region)
      if (mounted) {
        await AsyncStorage.setItem('markers_'+key, JSON.stringify(data))
        setMarkers(data)
      }
    }
    const t = setTimeout(fetchIfNeeded, 150)
    return () => { mounted = false; clearTimeout(t) }
  }, [region])
  return markers
}
```

